# Anomaly + Vulkan matches Anomaly + DX11

Anomaly is the pack host on both renderers. `Anomaly.Dx11` fulfills that host when the operational renderer is Keen DX11. SE-Vulkan's guest bus fulfills the same host when the operational renderer is Vulkan. Anomaly does not compile against either device. Packs do not compile against Anomaly. They read `ClientPlugin.Backend.RendererRoute` by reflection.

Anomaly-dependent plugins — DLSS, FRS, frame generation, HDR, aurora, clouds, shadows, Final Frontier, Prism, SE-RT, and the next pack — depend on that host. The dependency has to keep working when the route is Vulkan.

One shared contract: catalog names, `Fullscreen/<Slot>`, `anomaly.json`, `SetUniforms`, compose modes, and scale (1, 0.5, 0.25). `UseSharedBus` is open while the route is pending, on DX11, and on Vulkan. `UseDx11Device` is DX11 only. `UseGuestImages` is Vulkan only. A closed path is refused. Packs do not read SE-Vulkan `RequestedBackend` or `BackendRuntime`.

A shared-bus capability that exists on DX11 exists on the guest bus under the same names, or the call stays refused through `RendererRoute` until Anomaly owns the gap. Device work stays in `*.Dx11.dll`. Guest work is catalog images and fullscreen packets. Managed code does not record a `VkCommandBuffer` and does not touch `MyRender11` during a Vulkan session. SE-Vulkan does not grow a second pack registry.

A pack function that reads an Anomaly catalog buffer, claims a display service, or invalidates history on DX11 does the same on Vulkan. The renderer samples the guest image for that catalog name: velocity `0xFFFF00000000000A`, volumeReactive `0xFFFF00000000000B`, reactiveMask `0xFFFF00000000000C`. If the guest bus cannot publish that name yet, fill the Anomaly gap in the same turn and record it in `wiki/Framework-gaps.md`. Do not leave the Vulkan path on a renderer-private buffer while DX11 reads the catalog.

```text
# BAD
DX11 DLSS reads catalog velocity. Vulkan DLSS samples the renderer's object-motion image and ignores FrameTemporal.InvalidateHistory.
Pack detects Vulkan through SE-Vulkan internals and binds its own images.

# GOOD
Both backends read catalog velocity when history is valid, and both seed when InvalidateHistory clears it.
Pack registers, sets uniforms, and publishes on the shared bus.
DX11 device work waits for UseDx11Device; guest packets wait for UseGuestImages.
The same slot, catalog name, and compose mode work on both backends.
```
